    "order": "family given",
    "conventions": "Family name first, then a two-syllable given name: Chen Chia-hao, Lin Ya-ting. In Latin letters most people use the older Wade-Giles style spelling on their passport, with the given name hyphenated (Chen Chia-hao, not Chen Jiahao), so names here follow that. Chen and Lin are the commonest family names by far, then Huang, Chang, Li and Wang. Friends use the given name or add A- or Xiao- in front of one syllable (A-hao, Xiao-ting), and many people also go by an English name such as Kevin or Vivian, at school, at work and among friends.",
